WEBVTT

00:00:03.279 --> 00:00:09.230
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, all. Friday, first of May. Everyone on? I've got seven little squares and about three ceilings.</v>

00:00:09.869 --> 00:00:15.820
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, here. The heating in the portakabin is having a laugh. It's either tropical or absolutely Baltic.</v>

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.949
<v Marcus Hale>That's the temperature control: open the door, regret it, shut the door.</v>

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.460
<v Fiona Doyle>Pretty much. Anyway, that's a moan, not a maintenance request.</v>

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:33.880
<v Sarah Okafor>Before we start, the charity bake sale on Friday—that's today, despite what my brain says. Purely a reminder, no baking assignments.</v>

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.579
<v David Whitfield>Good. My contribution would need a COSHH sheet.</v>

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.850
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. Right, yesterday's bits first, then the actual work.</v>

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:49.609
<v Aisha Begum>I've already swapped the filter on the outfeed conveyor yesterday. That's finished, not something still hanging over today.</v>

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely, closed off then.</v>

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:59.420
<v Grace Liu>And I've already swapped the filter on the relief valve yesterday. Mine's done as well.</v>

00:01:00.409 --> 00:01:03.560
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you clipped there. That was completed yesterday, yeah?</v>

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.319
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, completed. Just reporting it, not asking for another go at it.</v>

00:01:11.769 --> 00:01:16.670
<v Fiona Doyle>One observation: heard a slight rattle from the GT2 bearing, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:21.209
<v David Whitfield>Right, just an observation, rather than another job going on the board?</v>

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:24.969
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:33.859
<v Aisha Begum>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve. That one's still blocked.</v>

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:42.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. That's the delivery blocker, separate from the risk assessment for work on the GT2 inlet valve we'll come to.</v>

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:50.010
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah. No delivery confirmation, so no change there. I'm not adding a chasing job this morning.</v>

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:55.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, the shutdown on the line 2 guard is cancelled now, production need it running.</v>

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.420
<v David Whitfield>The guard shutdown specifically, yeah? Not wiping every line 2 item off?</v>

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:06.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, just that shutdown. Cancelled, not parked as a job for later today.</v>

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:16.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha Begum, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the line 2 next week? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:18.199 --> 00:02:26.949
<v Aisha Begum>Just so I don't muddle that with the cancelled shutdown—next week is the due point, but you want that treated as an immediate safety priority?</v>

00:02:28.569 --> 00:02:35.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. Next week remains the due point. Straight away on priority; it doesn't mean isolate a running line right this second.</v>

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:45.580
<v Aisha Begum>Understood. I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the line 2 next week. Safety critical, straight away on that basis.</v>

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.400
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, that distinction matters. A cancelled shutdown isn't permission to blur the permit boundaries.</v>

00:02:53.599 --> 00:03:00.599
<v Sarah Okafor>And Aisha Begum, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve after lunch? It's urgent.</v>

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:07.229
<v Aisha Begum>Yes, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve after lunch. Understood it's urgent.</v>

00:03:08.289 --> 00:03:12.139
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, I was talking over you—did that move to before lunch?</v>

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.430
<v Aisha Begum>No, after lunch. Urgent, but the agreed timing is after lunch.</v>

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:23.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Davey, can you run a function test on the 11kV board this morning? Normal priority.</v>

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:29.610
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, accepted. I'll run a function test on the 11kV board this morning.</v>

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:36.460
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, normal priority, did you say? Audio went all underwater for a second.</v>

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Normal priority, yes. Not an emergency call-out.</v>

00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:44.020
<v David Whitfield>That's what I've got. This morning, normal priority.</v>

00:03:45.229 --> 00:03:50.129
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on spares, I'll order spare parts for the Water Booster Pump tomorrow.</v>

00:03:52.199 --> 00:03:56.050
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow as in Saturday? Sorry, bank holiday weekend's scrambled everyone's calendar.</v>

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:03.419
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, tomorrow, Saturday. I'll order them then. Not promising delivery tomorrow, just the order.</v>

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:08.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Marc. Ordering spare parts for the Water Booster Pump tomorrow, agreed.</v>

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:16.170
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona Doyle, can you clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer tomorrow at 9:30?</v>

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:24.420
<v Fiona Doyle>Yes, I'll take that. Clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.410
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, was that just the sensors? Teams swallowed the first half.</v>

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Both: clear the jam and check the sensors on the palletizer.</v>

00:04:34.339 --> 00:04:37.490
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, both parts accepted. I've got tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:39.029 --> 00:04:44.629
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll update the risk assessment for work on the GT2 inlet valve tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:51.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona. That risk assessment's not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:53.939 --> 00:05:02.689
<v Fiona Doyle>Agreed. I'll update the risk assessment for work on the GT2 inlet valve tomorrow at 9:30. Not an emergency, but I won't let it slip.</v>

00:05:04.329 --> 00:05:09.579
<v David Whitfield>You've got two against 9:30 there. Just checking that's deliberate, not me hearing an echo.</v>

00:05:10.689 --> 00:05:15.939
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, deliberate. Both are mine at the agreed time. I'm not asking to move either.</v>

00:05:18.319 --> 00:05:26.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Last one: Grace Liu, can you take vibration readings on the line 3 barrel by Wednesday? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:37.519
<v Grace Liu>I can't take that one, sorry. I haven't got the capacity to commit to it by Wednesday. Better say no now than nod and miss it.</v>

00:05:39.709 --> 00:05:42.160
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah Okafor, could you take that instead?</v>

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:51.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll take vibration readings on the line 3 barrel by Wednesday. Reassigned to me. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—understood.</v>

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:56.629
<v Grace Liu>Thanks. So that's off me and with Sarah Okafor, definitely?</v>

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Definitely. I'll own it, not you.</v>

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:05.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>The line 3 barrel, yeah? I'm getting every third noun this morning.</v>

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.199
<v Sarah Okafor>The line 3 barrel, yes. By Wednesday, with me.</v>

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:18.399
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's the agreed work. Anything I've mistaken for a live job that was only a status update?</v>

00:06:19.519 --> 00:06:26.870
<v Aisha Begum>Just keep the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve delivery marked blocked. Still no supplier confirmation, no new action agreed on that.</v>

00:06:28.149 --> 00:06:31.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Blocker only, not quietly allocating a chase to someone.</v>

00:06:31.949 --> 00:06:36.149
<v Fiona Doyle>And the GT2 bearing rattle stays an observation. Nothing to action yet.</v>

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:41.189
<v Grace Liu>Both yesterday's filter swaps are finished as well. No leftovers from those.</v>

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:48.100
<v David Whitfield>Good. A list that gets shorter as well as longer. Rare Friday treat.</v>

00:06:50.069 --> 00:06:55.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Don't jinx it. Thanks, everyone. That's us—enjoy the cakes if there's anything left beyond crumbs.</v>
